   <caption unique="1045960">Instruction Operand Encoding</caption>
   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1045962">Converts an unsigned doubleword integer (or unsigned quadword integer if operand size is 64 bits) in the second source operand to a double precision floating-point value in the destination operand. The result is stored in the low quadword of the destination operand. When conversion is inexact, the value returned is rounded according to the rounding control bits in the MXCSR register.</para>
  <para unique="1045963">The second source operand can be a general-purpose register or a 32/64-bit memory location. The first source and destination operands are XMM registers. Bits (127:64) of the XMM register destination are copied from corre&#173;sponding bits in the first source operand. Bits (MAXVL-1:128) of the destination register are zeroed.</para>
  <para unique="1045964">EVEX.W1 version: promotes the instruction to use 64-bit input value in 64-bit mode.</para>
  <para unique="1045965">EVEX.W0 version: attempt to encode this instruction with EVEX embedded rounding is ignored.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1045967">VCVTUSI2SD (EVEX Encoded Version)</title>
   <programlisting>IF (SRC2 *is register*) AND (EVEX.b = 1)
	THEN
		SET_ROUNDING_MODE_FOR_THIS_INSTRUCTION(EVEX.RC);
	ELSE
		SET_ROUNDING_MODE_FOR_THIS_INSTRUCTION(MXCSR.RC);
FI;
IF 64-Bit Mode And OperandSize = 64
THEN
	DEST[63:0] := Convert_UInteger_To_Double_Precision_Floating_Point(SRC2[63:0]);
ELSE
	DEST[63:0] := Convert_UInteger_To_Double_Precision_Floating_Point(SRC2[31:0]);
FI;
DEST[127:64] := SRC1[127:64]
DEST[MAXVL-1:128] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>VCVTUSI2SD __m128d _mm_cvtu32_sd( __m128d s, unsigned a);
VCVTUSI2SD __m128d _mm_cvtu64_sd( __m128d s, unsigned __int64 a);
VCVTUSI2SD __m128d _mm_cvt_roundu64_sd( __m128d s, unsigned __int64 a, int r);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1045987">Precision.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1045994" format="xIndent1">See <link unique="1045990" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#71006: 06_Table: Table 2-48. Type E3NF Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page">Table&#160;2&#8209;50, &#8220;Type E3NF Class Exception Conditions&#8221;</link> if W1; otherwise, see <link unique="1045993" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#87248: 06_Table: Table 2-59. Type E10NF Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page with period">Table&#160;2&#8209;61, &#8220;Type E10NF Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
